    {
      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Solar Energy (Photovoltaic and Thermal)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Photovoltaic (PV) cells convert sunlight directly into electricity through the photovoltaic effect, while solar thermal systems use the sun's heat to warm water or air for heating purposes.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"As of 2024, solar energy accounts for approximately 4-5% of global electricity generation, with rapid growth rates of 15-25% annually in recent years.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/solar-pv-global-supply-chains\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The levelized cost of electricity (LCOE) from utility-scale solar PV has declined by approximately 89% between 2010 and 2020, making it one of the cheapest electricity sources.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021-Jun/Renewable-Cost-Database\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Silicon-based solar cells dominate the global PV market, accounting for approximately 95% of all commercial solar panels, with monocrystalline and polycrystalline variants being most common.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/solar-pv-global-supply-chains\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems can achieve efficiency rates of 50-80% in converting solar radiation to usable heat, while photovoltaic systems typically achieve 15-22% electrical conversion efficiency in commercial applications.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"China leads global solar PV capacity installation with over 400 GW installed as of 2023, followed by the European Union, United States, Japan, and India.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/statistics/electricity\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Emerging PV technologies including perovskite solar cells, tandem solar cells, and thin-film technologies are in development stages with potential efficiencies exceeding 30% in laboratory conditions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems are widely used for residential water heating, space heating, and industrial process heat applications, with significant deployment in countries like Austria, Germany, and Australia.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.solarthermalworld.org/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) systems use mirrors to concentrate sunlight and generate heat for electricity production, with some installations featuring thermal storage capabilities allowing energy generation after sunset.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The International Energy Agency projects that solar will be the world's leading source of electricity by 2050, requiring cumulative investments of approximately $4 trillion through 2050.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/solar-pv-global-supply-chains\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
