      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Biomass and Biofuel Technologies\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Biomass accounts for approximately 15% of global energy consumption, making it the largest renewable energy source worldwide.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/biomass-for-heating\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Biofuels can be categorized into first-generation (from food crops), second-generation (from waste and residues), and advanced biofuels (from algae and other sources).\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/bioenergy/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global biofuel production reached approximately 162 billion liters in 2022, with biodiesel and bioethanol being the dominant types.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/statistics/biofuels\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Second-generation biofuels from lignocellulosic biomass can reduce greenhouse gas emissions by up to 90% compared to fossil fuels.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/advanced-biofuels\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Anaerobic digestion of biomass can produce biogas (methane) for energy generation while reducing methane emissions from landfills.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Dec/Biogas-technology-brief\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The European Union targets 42.5% renewable energy by 2030, with bioenergy expected to contribute significantly to this goal.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.europarl.europa.eu/news/en/headlines/society/2022\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Biochar, produced from biomass pyrolysis, can improve soil carbon storage and crop productivity while sequestering carbon.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41561-020-00664-2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Algae-based biofuels have the potential to produce 5-15 times more biomass per acre than terrestrial crops like soybeans or palm.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/bioenergy/algae-to-biofuels.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
