      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Hybrid and Integrated Renewable Systems\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hybrid renewable systems combine two or more renewable energy sources (such as solar, wind, and hydroelectric) with energy storage to provide continuous power generation and improve grid reliability.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.int/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Integrated renewable energy systems can reduce energy costs by 20-30% compared to single-source renewable systems through complementary generation patterns and optimized resource utilization.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar-wind hybrid systems are particularly effective because solar generation peaks during midday while wind generation often increases during evening and night hours, providing complementary generation profiles.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery energy storage systems (BESS) are critical components in hybrid renewable systems, with lithium-ion batteries currently dominating the market due to declining costs and improved performance.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Microgrids incorporating hybrid renewable systems can operate independently from the main grid during outages, enhancing energy resilience in remote and rural communities.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/microgrid\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart grid technologies and advanced power management systems are essential for optimizing the operation and dispatch of integrated renewable energy systems.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.smartgrid.gov/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Denmark generates approximately 80% of its electricity from wind and hydroelectric power through an integrated Nordic renewable system approach.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://en.energinet.dk/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pumped hydro storage systems serve as effective long-duration energy storage in hybrid renewable systems, providing storage capacity of 24-48 hours or more.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.int/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydrogen production through electrolysis of renewable energy is emerging as an integration technology to store excess renewable energy for long-term use.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/hydrogen\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Virtual power plants (VPPs) aggregate multiple distributed renewable energy resources and flexible loads to operate as a single controllable entity on the grid.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
