      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Energy Storage Systems\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery energy storage systems (BESS) are the fastest-growing energy storage technology, with global capacity expected to reach 2,700 GWh by 2030 according to the International Energy Agency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/battery-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Lithium-ion batteries currently dominate the energy storage market, accounting for approximately 95% of all battery energy storage deployments globally as of 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/battery-technology-basics\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pumped-storage hydroelectricity remains the largest deployed energy storage technology worldwide, accounting for over 90% of global energy storage capacity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/articles/energy-storage-basics\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Long-duration energy storage systems (8+ hours) including thermal storage, compressed air energy storage (CAES), and flow batteries are critical for grid stability and managing renewable energy variability\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy21osti/79278.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Vanadium redox flow batteries can store energy for 10+ hours and have cycle lives exceeding 20,000 charge-discharge cycles, making them suitable for long-duration applications\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/energy-storage-system-basics\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global energy storage deployment increased 35% year-over-year in 2022, with battery storage capacity reaching 13 GW according to the International Energy Agency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/battery-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Thermal energy storage systems can integrate with concentrated solar power (CSP) plants to enable electricity generation after sunset, with some systems storing heat for 15+ hours\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/csp/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Gravity energy storage systems are emerging as a non-chemical alternative, using weights or concrete blocks to store energy through elevation changes\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/energy-storage-basics\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
