      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Waste-to-Energy Technologies\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Waste-to-Energy (WtE) technologies convert non-recyclable waste into usable heat and electricity through various processes including incineration, gasification, anaerobic digestion, and pyrolysis\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.epa.gov/energy/waste-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"According to the International Energy Agency, waste-to-energy facilities worldwide prevent approximately 10% of global waste from going to landfills while generating renewable energy\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/waste-to-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Anaerobic digestion of organic waste produces biogas (primarily methane and carbon dioxide) that can be used to generate electricity or heat, with typical conversion efficiency of 20-30%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.epa.gov/anaerobic-digestion\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Modern waste-to-energy incineration facilities equipped with advanced pollution control systems emit significantly less harmful compounds than older facilities and comply with strict environmental regulations\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/waste-energy-technologies\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Europe leads in waste-to-energy adoption with over 500 WtE plants operating across the continent, treating approximately 13% of municipal waste\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.confederation-cfe.eu/topics/waste-to-energy/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pyrolysis and gasification technologies can process waste at lower temperatures than traditional incineration and produce syngas that can be converted to electricity or biofuels\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy14osti/61143.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global waste-to-energy market was valued at approximately $30-35 billion in 2022 and is expected to grow at a compound annual growth rate of 5-7% through 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/waste-to-energy-market\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Waste-to-energy facilities can achieve overall energy efficiency rates of 60-80% when combined heat and power (CHP) systems are utilized\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/combined-heat-and-power\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
