      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Seasonal Thermal Storage\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Seasonal thermal storage systems store thermal energy during periods of excess heat production (typically summer) for use during periods of heat demand (typically winter), with storage durations of several months\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S036054421400169X\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Aquifer thermal energy storage (ATES) is a mature technology that uses natural or artificial aquifers to store hot or cold water, with proven applications in multiple countries including the Netherlands, Sweden, and Canada\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0960148116302725\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Borehole thermal energy storage (BTES) systems can achieve round-trip efficiencies of 50-90% depending on design and geological conditions\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0196890416303855\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Underground thermal energy storage can reduce renewable heat system costs by 20-40% when integrated with district heating networks\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360544216309690\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pit thermal energy storage and tank thermal energy storage are cost-effective alternatives for seasonal storage with lower drilling costs than borehole systems\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038092X19311119\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Phase change materials (PCMs) can increase thermal storage capacity density, though they face challenges with thermal cycling degradation and higher material costs\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306261918314387\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Seasonal thermal storage coupled with solar thermal systems can meet 50-100% of annual heating demands in European climates\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038092X18301026\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Thermochemical storage systems using salt hydrates or other reversible chemical reactions can achieve higher energy density than sensible heat storage but remain largely in research and pilot phases\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0196890415007487\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"District heating networks integrated with seasonal thermal storage can reduce greenhouse gas emissions by 50-80% compared to fossil fuel alternatives\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0959652618309569\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The main barriers to seasonal thermal storage deployment are high capital costs, long payback periods (10-20 years), and limited technical expertise in design and installation\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306261918307573\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
