      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Renewable Energy Policy and Economics\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The Inflation Reduction Act (IRA), signed into law in August 2022, provides $369 billion in clean energy and climate investments, making it the largest climate investment in U.S. history with tax credits for solar, wind, and battery storage\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/inflation-reduction-act-energy-security-climate-crisis\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"According to the International Energy Agency (IEA), renewable energy is projected to provide over 42% of global electricity by 2050 under current policy scenarios\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/renewable-energy-market-update\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The levelized cost of electricity (LCOE) for solar photovoltaic and onshore wind has declined by approximately 89% and 70% respectively between 2010-2021\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Jul/Renewable-Power-Generation-Costs-in-2022\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The European Union's Renewable Energy Directive (RED IV) aims for 42.5% renewable energy in gross final consumption by 2030, up from previous targets\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/energy/topics/renewable-energy/directive-targets-and-rules_en\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Feed-in tariffs and power purchase agreements (PPAs) are major policy mechanisms that guarantee renewable energy producers fixed prices for electricity, reducing investment risk\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Jun/Renewable-Energy-Policy-Framework\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global renewable energy capacity additions reached 295 GW in 2022, with solar and wind accounting for approximately 90% of new capacity additions\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2023/Apr/Renewable-Capacity-Statistics-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"China leads global renewable energy investment, spending approximately $546 billion on clean energy in 2022, accounting for about one-third of global renewable energy spending\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/news/global-renewable-energy-investment-hits-record-high-in-2022\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Subsidy removal and carbon pricing mechanisms are increasingly used by policymakers to improve the economic competitiveness of renewable energy against fossil fuels\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.worldbank.org/en/topic/extractiveindustries/brief/fossil-fuel-subsidies\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
