      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Environmental and Social Impact Assessment for Renewable Energy Technologies\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Environmental and Social Impact Assessments (ESIAs) are systematic processes used to evaluate the potential environmental and social effects of proposed renewable energy projects before implementation, including solar, wind, hydro, and geothermal installations.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.ifc.org/en/insights-updates/news/2020/environmental-and-social-impact-assessment\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar photovoltaic installations can have significant land-use impacts, affecting ecosystems and biodiversity, particularly when deployed at utility scale, requiring careful site selection and environmental assessment.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy21osti/80580.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Wind energy projects must assess impacts on bird and bat populations, with migratory routes and sensitive habitats requiring particular attention during environmental impact assessments.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.audubon.org/conservation/birds-and-renewable-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydroelectric power projects create significant social impacts including displacement of communities, changes to water resources, and alterations to aquatic ecosystems that require comprehensive social and environmental assessments.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.worldwildlife.org/publications/dams-and-development-relevant-framework-for-decision-making\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Renewable energy projects require assessments of cumulative impacts, considering how multiple projects in a region interact with existing environmental and social conditions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/environmental-and-social-impact-of-renewable-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Local community engagement and free, prior, and informed consent (FPIC) processes are critical components of social impact assessments for renewable energy projects, particularly in areas with indigenous populations.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.undp.org/publications/indigenous-peoples-renewable-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Supply chain impacts, including mining for rare earth elements and battery materials required for renewable energy storage and grid integration, must be included in comprehensive environmental and social assessments.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/the-role-of-critical-minerals-in-clean-energy-transitions\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"International standards and frameworks such as IFC Performance Standards and the World Bank Environmental and Social Framework provide guidance for conducting ESIAs for renewable energy projects in developing countries.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.worldbank.org/en/topic/environmental-and-social-framework\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Geothermal energy development requires assessments of induced seismicity risks, subsurface fluid interactions, and potential impacts on hot springs and geothermal resources used by local communities.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.usgs.gov/programs/vhp/geothermal-energy-and-seismicity\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Renewable energy projects in marine environments, including offshore wind and tidal installations, require specialized environmental assessments addressing marine biodiversity, shipping routes, and commercial fisheries impacts.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.noaa.gov/media/offshore-wind-environmental-assessment\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
