      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Energy Efficiency and Demand Management\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Energy efficiency improvements can reduce overall energy demand by 20-30% in buildings through better insulation, HVAC systems, and LED lighting\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-efficiency-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Demand response programs enable consumers to adjust electricity consumption during peak hours, reducing strain on grids and lowering overall system costs by 5-15%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy14osti/61721.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart meters and advanced metering infrastructure (AMI) provide real-time energy consumption data that can support demand management and reduce peak loads\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/smart-grid\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Industrial energy efficiency improvements, particularly in manufacturing, can reduce energy consumption by 10-25% through process optimization and equipment upgrades\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/energy-efficiency-in-industry\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Demand-side management programs integrated with renewable energy systems improve renewable penetration rates by reducing variability in net electricity demand\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy12osti/55960.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Time-of-use (TOU) electricity pricing encourages consumers to shift consumption away from peak hours, reducing peak demand by 5-10%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.eia.gov/analysis/studies/electricity/pdf/time-of-use.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Building energy management systems can optimize HVAC, lighting, and other loads autonomously, achieving 15-25% energy savings\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.greenbuildingadvisor.com/article/building-energy-management-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Energy storage systems paired with demand management can help balance intermittent renewable generation by storing excess power during low-demand periods\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/72283.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Electric vehicle charging management represents an emerging demand flexibility resource that can shift up to 50% of charging loads to off-peak hours\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy20osti/75237.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Behavioral interventions and consumer feedback mechanisms can reduce household energy consumption by 1.5-3% without technological modifications\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1080/15568318.2015.1033945\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
