{
  "id": "msg_011Cf7asH8Epi897E4QLcvpx",
  "container": null,
  "content": [
    {
      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Solar Energy (Photovoltaic and Thermal)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Photovoltaic (PV) cells convert sunlight directly into electricity using the photovoltaic effect, where photons knock electrons loose from atoms in silicon or other semiconductor materials.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/photovoltaics\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems use the sun's heat directly for applications such as heating water, space heating, and industrial processes, distinct from photovoltaic systems that generate electricity.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/solar-thermal-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"As of 2024, solar energy accounts for approximately 4-5% of global electricity generation, with rapid growth in deployment across residential, commercial, and utility-scale installations.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/energy-system/renewables/solar-pv-and-solar-thermal\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Modern commercial silicon PV panels typically have efficiency ratings between 15-22%, while laboratory prototypes using multi-junction cells have achieved efficiencies exceeding 40%.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal collectors can achieve energy conversion efficiencies of 50-80%, making them highly efficient for heating applications compared to photovoltaic systems.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/solar-thermal-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global installed capacity of solar PV reached approximately 1.4 terawatts (TW) by the end of 2023, representing the fastest-growing renewable energy technology worldwide.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/solar-pv-global-supply-chains\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar panel costs have declined by approximately 89% over the past decade (2014-2024), significantly improving the economic competitiveness of solar energy.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2024/Mar/Renewable-power-generation-costs-2024\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) systems use mirrors or lenses to concentrate sunlight and generate heat for electricity production, with some facilities incorporating thermal storage for 24-hour operation.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/concentrating-solar-power\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells, an emerging technology, have demonstrated laboratory efficiencies exceeding 33% and offer potential advantages in manufacturing costs and flexibility compared to traditional silicon cells.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery storage integration with solar PV systems is becoming increasingly common, with global battery storage capacity paired with solar expected to grow significantly through 2030.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/battery-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
