      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Advanced Nuclear (SMRs and Next-Gen)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Small Modular Reactors (SMRs) are nuclear reactors with electrical output capacity of 300 MW or less per unit, designed for smaller grids and industrial applications\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/energy-system/nuclear-power-and-security/small-modular-reactors\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"NuScale Power received the first U.S. design certification for an SMR from the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) in September 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nuscalepower.com/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) reported over 70 SMR designs under development globally as of 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iaea.org/newscenter/news/what-are-small-modular-reactors-smrs\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Next-generation nuclear technologies include advanced fast reactors, molten salt reactors, and high-temperature gas-cooled reactors (HTGCRs) designed to improve safety and fuel efficiency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/ne/advanced-reactor-demonstration-program\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The U.S. Department of Energy's Advanced Reactor Demonstration Program (ARDP) is funding projects to deploy advanced reactors, including support for TerraPower's sodium-cooled fast reactor demonstration\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/ne/advanced-reactor-demonstration-program\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"SMRs have lower upfront capital costs per unit than large conventional nuclear plants, though higher cost per MW of capacity due to economies of scale\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/energy-system/nuclear-power-and-security/small-modular-reactors\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Several countries including China, Russia, and France are actively developing and deploying SMR technologies, with Russia operating the Akademik Lomonosov floating SMR unit since 2020\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iaea.org/newscenter/news/what-are-small-modular-reactors-smrs\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Next-generation reactors are designed to operate at higher temperatures than traditional light-water reactors, enabling potential applications in industrial heat and hydrogen production\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/ne/advanced-reactor-demonstration-program\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"SMRs can be deployed in remote locations and off-grid applications, and have potential for district heating and desalination applications\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iaea.org/newscenter/news/what-are-small-modular-reactors-smrs\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"X-energy's Xe-100 high-temperature gas reactor and Oklo's Aurora microreactor are among next-generation projects receiving U.S. government funding\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/ne/advanced-reactor-demonstration-program\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
